# Play4Cash PWA — Session & Auth Contract

This repo is the React + Vite PWA. The session architecture was hardened in a multi-repo
sweep across `Play4CashPWA`, `Play4CashApi`, and `Play4CashGateway`. Keep these invariants
when editing auth/session/socket code.

## Tokens

- **Access token**: in-memory only (`accessTokenMem` in `src/data/auth/AuthSessionStore.ts`).
  Never persisted to `localStorage`. `saveTokens(token)` sets memory and bumps a cross-tab
  signal; `getAccessToken()` returns the in-memory value; `getRefreshToken()` is a deprecated
  no-op kept for back-compat.
- **Refresh token**: lives in an **httpOnly cookie** set by the API. JS can't read it. All
  Axios clients use `withCredentials: true`. The SPA calls `POST /api/login/refresh` with no
  body — the cookie travels automatically.
- **Logout**: calls `apiRepository.logout()` then `requestRefreshCookieCleared()` to invalidate
  the cookie, plus `clearTokens()` + `clearRoutingContext()`.

## Routing & hydration

- Route protection in `src/auth/RequireAuth.tsx`. `RequireAuth` waits for `authHydrated`
  (set by `authStore.loadSession`) before redirecting to `/login`.
- `RootRedirect` handles `/` and `*` based on hydrated user state.

## Cross-tab sync

- Primary: `BroadcastChannel('p4c-auth')` with kinds `login | refresh | logout`. See
  `onAuthBroadcast` in `AuthSessionStore.ts`.
- Fallback: a `p4c_session_version` key in `localStorage` is bumped on every auth change so
  the `storage` event fires in browsers without BroadcastChannel.
- The listener in `authStore.ts` debounces both sources into a single `loadSession()` call.

## Sockets

- Token still goes in the WS handshake query (`?token=…`) — the Gateway needs it because the
  browser cannot set `Authorization` on a WebSocket upgrade.
- All `*SocketManager.ts` files reuse `src/data/network/socketSessionRefresh.ts`:
  `isSocketUnauthorizedConnectError` + `refreshSocketHandshake` (which calls
  `refreshAccessTokenWithLock` from `ApiClient.ts`). **Don't duplicate this logic** in new
  managers.

## Dev proxy

- `vite.config.ts` reads `VITE_DEV_PROXY_TARGET` (+ `VITE_DEV_PROXY_INSECURE`). When set,
  `/api` and `/socket.io` are proxied to the target so the SPA shares the API's origin in
  dev. Leave `VITE_API_URL` empty in that case.
- `BASE_URL` in `src/config/api.config.ts` falls back to `''` in dev (relative) and the prod
  URL otherwise.

## Forbidden patterns

- ❌ Saving access tokens to `localStorage`/`sessionStorage`.
- ❌ Reading the refresh token in JS (it's httpOnly).
- ❌ Per-manager copies of socket-refresh logic.
- ❌ Removing `withCredentials: true` from any client that hits `/api/login*` or `/api/logout`.

